==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|vinr}}, {{der|is|gem-pro|*winiz}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*wenh₁-||to seek, desire, love, win}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈvɪːnʏr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɪːnʏr|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# [[friend]]
#: {{syn|is|máti|félagi|kumpáni}}
#: {{ux|is|Þú ert '''vinur''' minn.|You are my '''friend'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Þú ert góður '''vinur'''.|You are a good '''friend'''.}}
# {{lb|is|colloquial|slang|somewhat old-fashioned|often used with a definite article}} [[mate]], [[lad]], an affectionate moniker for a close [[friend]] or [[pal]], especially used as a form of [[address]]
#: {{syn|is|kall<qq:often in the definite form {{m|is|kallinn}}>|gaur|kjell<qq:often in the definite form {{m|is|kjellinn}}>}}
#: {{ux|is|[[jæja|Jæja]] '''vinurinn''', ætli maður fari ekki að [[koma sér af stað]].|Well '''mate''', I guess we should [[get going]].}}

